# ==============================================================
# Shared blood DNA methylation signatures of comorbid disorders - five-disorder panel
# Step 53: figures for submission, all generated directly from the analysis output
#
# The figures of earlier reports and drafts were drawn separately from numbers in the logs. Figures for submission must be produced by
# the analysis pipeline itself: for re-analyses of public data the journal requires code that reproduces the results, and the figures should be generated by
# the same code. This step only reads existing output and recomputes no model.
#
# Six main figures:
#   Fig1  study design: sample numbers per cohort and analysis workflow
#   Fig2  within-disease replication: effect-size scatter (five disorders, with a quantile trend strip below), ten-thousand-permutation nulls, detection limits
#   Fig3  cross-disease comparison: summary matrix, the forty pairings, effect-size scatter of the highest cross-disease cell
#   Fig4  calibration by sex: comparison of three groups, same vs different platform, distribution per cohort
#   Fig5  leukocyte composition: effect heat map (ten sets x twelve types), loadings of the direction common to the cohorts, before and after its removal (leave-out)
#   Fig6  overlap approach vs calibrated criterion: comparison over the forty-five pairs (computed in this step, exploratory)
# Six supplementary figures:
#   FigS1 inflation factor and number of principal components per cohort
#   FigS2 principal component diagnosis of GSE198904
#   FigS3 robustness to region aggregation and to the quality covariate
#   FigS4 sample-level checks (sex concordance, bimodality index and its association with group)
#   FigS5 genetic correlation category and methylation concordance
#   FigS6 cross-disease summary matrix of the composition axis
#
# Three self-checks are run; if any fails the script stops and produces no figure:
#   (1) the common direction and the correlations before and after its removal, recomputed from the composition effects, agree with the results saved by step 40;
#   (2) the within-disease Spearman correlations recomputed from the effect vectors agree with the values recorded by step 45;
#   (3) the inflation factors recomputed from the t statistics agree with the table of frozen settings (tolerance 0.01).
# The plotted data of every figure are also written as CSV, as the source data required by the journal.
#
# Figure specifications (submission requirements of Clinical Epigenetics): Arial, full width 170 mm, half width 85 mm, height at most 225 mm,
#   body font size 7 pt, vector PDF and 600 dpi TIFF (LZW compression).
#
# Environment: Windows + RStudio. Reads the ten effect vectors, about ten minutes
# Location: <project root>/scripts/53_manuscript_figures.R
# ==============================================================

PROJ_ROOT <- "C:/blood_methylation_project"
